![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The handheld chimes. A pale line of light passes from it across the woman’s temple, then fades. Her struggle stops. She blinks at Asha, confused, and looks around the room as if she has no idea how she got there.

Inuran Woman (Educator):Whatever cruel demeanor had previously possessed the Inuran before you is completely gone now, replaced by the strangest, innocent confusion. She just stares, not exactly sure what is happening, who she is, or why.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"Easy," she says, glancing between both of them. "Grab the equipment and let's go. I don't think we set off any alarms yet."

Inuran Woman (Educator):"Alarms?"

"Are we friends?"

Asha Morrow:"Dear friends, we got to you a moment too late." Asha grabs a set of equipment and holds it out in front of the woman, "Hold this for a moment."

Inuran Woman (Educator):She wraps her arms around the box and holds onto it, clearly trying to wrap her mind around this and failing.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"Don't you worry a thing. You'll remember what's going on soon, okay? You're safe here."

Inuran Woman (Educator):"I... don’t know what’s going on. I'll follow your lead."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina secures a box as well and heads for the door. "All right, nice and cool now. Everyone ready?"

Inuran Woman (Educator):She stares at Asha, and then Kaelith, then back to Asha. "What am I doing with this?"

Asha Morrow:Asha shoots Kaelith and glance, "Just hold it for now. It'll make sense later. Let's move."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Got it boss. Right behind you."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Yraina leads the group back through the quiet corridor. Staff glance up as they pass, then return to their work. The wipe follows with the box held against her chest. The corridor opens into the pale reception area where an attendant sits behind the long counter, his display suspended before him. Two people in plain work clothes still wait along the far wall among the empty chairs. The attendant looks up as you approach, then lowers his gaze to the display. The glass doors unlock for you without a word.

Unless you choose to interrupt, you all end up back on the ramp outside, walking at a good pace back to your ship with the woman in tow.

Asha Morrow:Asha plays it cool.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith strides along with purpose and confidence_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The ship's cargo ramp swallows you back up and seals behind you, allowing everyone to let go of any tension of being caught on the way back. The bay itself feels emptier even though most of the crew is still here. Smoke's constant presence is replaced by a different way of leading the crew. Bell is filling in for him at the moment. She is currently speaking with one of the gravity hover tank crews who all look kitted out and ready to fight if needed.

Past the cargo bay and onto the bridge, the only one to be found there is Nyrix; she is at the communications station, keeping watch. Through the windows, the remote port’s hard lights fall across the hull and scattered service buildings.

Asha Morrow:"Can someone get us the fuck out of here while the gettin's good." Asha grabs the equipment from the blank woman and finds a spot for it for the moment.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith makes way for his Matrix rings and prepares in the event something drastic is needed_

Asha Morrow:Asha realizes the bridge is less full than usual and shakes her head, moving into position to be the one to maneuver them out.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Nyrix hurries into the pilot’s seat, eager to get moving. She checks the startup sequence twice, then lifts the Lone Star from the pad. The ship tilts as it rises; Nyrix corrects too sharply, then steadies it and guides the ship away from the port.

Asha Morrow:"Oh hey, have you been practicing?"

Inuran Woman (Educator):She goes to stare out the bridge window, just enraptured and also probably trying to figure out where she is.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix brightens. "A little! I’ve been practicing the takeoff sequence. That counts, right?" She keeps both hands on the controls and watches the ship’s path closely.

Asha Morrow:"It does count!"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina leans back against the large holographic display and crosses her arms, one foot tapping as she thinks.

"Once Nyrix gets us clear of the port, we head for Maena's headquarters. Before any wipe, I’ll record and verify your imprints. Nyrix can keep the duplicate copies and another kit aboard, along with the gear we’ll need to retrieve afterward."

Asha Morrow:"Yes and what about that one." Asha gestures subtly towards the blank woman.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina watches her with a look of pity. "Maybe just feed her and keep her under watch here until the operation is over."

Asha Morrow:Asha goes to call up Smoke, remembers, and calls Bell instead. "Got a job for you..well, no way to sell it better its basically babysitting. There's a woman here that'll need to be looked after and could probably use some socialization at the same time."

Bell Delatii:"We'll handle it. I saw her when you arrived. Coming by to scoop her up now."

Bell is at the bridge in record time and there's an indicator to Asha that she has requested to board.

