Asha Morrow:Asha takes piloting from Nyrix with an appreciative smile and sets their course to the Maena HQ, double checking with Yraina that she has it all right. "Walk us through this again. When do we need to wipe?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:She replies to Asha. "Yeah, this is the hard part now, and I'm going to need you two to take the lead once we're inside. We'll take a backup of both of you, double check it, make a copy, and then I'll walk you in as personal servants. That will get us into the review and into a quiet space where I can restore you two. The review just gets us into holding though, not wherever we want. From there, we look for the research and executive records to find out what Maena is building and why they need Spark. The public directory calls the lab '_Reserve Compatibility_', so let's keep our eyes out for that. That's all I know."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix doesn't resist, not that she could override Asha's control anyway of the ship. She leans back and listens.

Asha Morrow:"Alright, let's do that part now before we arrive. I don't want to rush this."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The entire routine takes only moments. Yraina shows you a blank wafer, "This is where it ends up." She places it into the slot in the box and then removes the handheld. The end of it is a smooth, rounded metallic probe covered in magitech circuitry. "I push the backup on this, and then touch it to your head and a few moments later you're done. You can even do it yourself." She offers the first one to Asha.

Asha Morrow:"Fuck no, just do it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina slowly reaches forward and taps the end of it against Asha's forehead. There is almost no sensation to it, and then a couple moments later she straightens up. "Okay, backup loaded."

She swaps the wafer out for a new blank and then looks to Kaelith. She offers him the device.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith takes the wafer and looks it over_ "This shit is so fucked up." _He lets it slide down into his palm and then smacks it to his forehead_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"Yeah... there's nothing good about this work," she replies. The handheld softly chimes a few moments later. "And now Kaelith is loaded."

She takes both wafers and makes a copy of each, then offers them to Nyrix. "Keep these safe in case something happens to us. I'm also planning to contact you within thirty minutes of us going in, so if you don't hear from me then assume we're compromised."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix takes them and nods with a fierce look. "I know what to do."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"The other two wafers stay in the box. I'll check those in with me. Now you two just have to wipe yourselves once you're ready. Same procedure, just... swap the button on the handheld."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith takes Axiom in hand and opens a void pocket to place him inside for safe keeping, then grabs the handheld and flips the switch and engages it_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The Lone Star starts its approach just then. Maena’s headquarters sits in a recessed commercial block beside the Trade Moon’s freight concourse, its polished visitor frontage set back from the loading lanes. The Lone Star settles onto a nearby service pad as cargo haulers roll past the marked court. Through the windows, you can make out sales offices, sample displays, and appointment desks at the front of the building. Beyond them, staff and freight move through separate doors deeper inside.

The handheld in Kaelith's hand buzzes softly indicating that it's ready. Into the void.

Asha Morrow:A pit opens in Asha's stomach as the moment of truth comes, every part of her being is screaming at her not to do this. But she will.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:What exactly Kaelith experiences is a mystery to all but him as he engages the device. One moment he's there, then with a soft chime he is gone. All knowledge of magic. Every memory, name, anything but the basics. He knows what a gun is, but not if he can fire it for example. Whoever Kaelith was is blown away like the wind.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina walks up to him and reaches out to gently take the device from him.

"How are you feeling?" she asks as she does so.

Asha Morrow:Asha holds her hand out for the device, "Don't give me too much time to think about this."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina offers the device to Asha then.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I feel fine. But where am I? What am i doing on a spaceship?"

Asha Morrow:Asha takes the device, presses it against her temple, and in a certain sense kills herself.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"Okay sorry, I was waiting until our friend here joined you." Yraina paces back to stare at both of them, arms on her hips. "You two are too damn smart to get tripped up on this so I'm just going to give it to you straight. Nod your head if you're with me."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix watches this all in cool amusement.

Asha Morrow:Asha stares at the woman, looks around the room, then back to the woman and nods every so slightly.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith shrugs his shoulders and looks around, then nods in agreement_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"We are friends, and you're on an important mission to save the galaxy. You wiped your own memories for this phase of the operation so you can pretend to be personal servants. I need you to endure about thirty minutes of wild confusion and hold it together. On the other side you'll wake up and feel normal again. Questions?"

Asha Morrow:Asha's face contorts in confusion and she swallows hard. She look over at Kaelith, then back around the room, and finally back to Yraina to respond quietly "Okay..."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks himself over and seeing his high quality attire and jewelry, is satisfied with Yraina's commentary_ "Sounds like something I would do. I'm in."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:She suddenly starts laughing.

"You two are surprisingly not all that different. Good. Okay, try your best to just buckle the fuck up and enjoy seeing things with brand new eyes for a few minutes. If you're ready then just follow me, I'll lead us in."

She walks past both of them toward the exit of the bridge and waits there.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:Nyrix silently stares, looking perhaps unsettling in her uncanny form. A good attempt at human, but the hair is not quite the right texture, and the eyes are clearly draconic, along with the complete lack of imperfections.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith turns and follows in tow_

Asha Morrow:Asha stands up and stares back at Nyrix, forgetting for a moment what she was supposed to do. "You're beautiful.." she mumbles without really meaning to

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:She clutches her heart with one hand and smiles back at Asha. "I'll see you later," she replies with a wink.

Asha Morrow:Asha's face scrunches again and she goes to follow Yraina.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"And don't worry about names for now, you're not going to need them," she says as they walk.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"OK"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Inside, the visitor hall is bright and carefully arranged. The floors are polished and matched with clean, pale walls, and glass displays holding compact magitech devices beside neat product cards. Appointment screens and freight schedules share a wall, giving the place the tidy feel of a manufacturer that expects customers and shipments.

Yraina leads you across the visitor frontage, past sample displays and freight schedules, to a receptionist’s counter. The receptionist asks for your business.

"Household referral," Yraina says. "I'm sponsoring two personal servants, and I’m declaring a restoration kit."

The receptionist checks Yraina’s identity, records the referral, and directs you to wait for the next entry cycle.

Beyond the counter, a vast circular vault door fills the wall. A sign above it reads **ONE GROUP PER CYCLE**. Before the door, a magitech arch waits beside a narrow strip of floor. When the group ahead clears the chamber, the receptionist signals you forward.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina pauses just before the arch and takes a breath before stepping through it.

Asha Morrow:Asha is basically staring at everything and waiting for Yraina's cue to do anything, following closely behind whenever she moves.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith, much like Asha just stares around at all the sights and sounds_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:A pale light passes over each of you, while fine symbols scroll across the arch’s display: NO OBVIOUS SPIRIT BINDINGS DETECTED.

The vault door rolls aside. Yraina leads you into a broad, bare chamber; the door closes behind you with a deep mechanical clunk. After a brief pause, the inner door unlocks and opens onto a staffed household intake desk.

A registrar looks up from her screen. "Sponsor’s name and household destination?" Yraina gives her name and asks for household review. The registrar checks the record, then gestures to a marked equipment tray. "Please declare the restoration kit while I verify the referral." Past the desk, separate doors lead to household review and other internal departments. Each has its own credential reader and staff station. The **Reserve Compatibility** directory is visible beyond the next secured passage, but your referral has not opened it.

Neris verifies Yraina in the household records, logs her as the sponsor, and refers the personal-servant claim for review. She issues one sponsor band and two dependent bands which are placed around your wrists, then sends you to a household consultation room while the review is pending. The restoration kit is declared and checked for safe handling and allowed to go through with Yraina.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The room has three chairs, a wash station, a door-status panel, and a call button for household review. Its occupancy sensor and door log register who enters and leaves, but there’s no live audio or memory feed. The worker who escorted them here estimates the review will take fifteen minutes and says an interviewer or escort will come to the door soon to pick them up.

Otherwise, they are left alone.

